<p><strong>Structural Self-Energy Expansion (SSEE)</strong> asks whether the shape of late-time cosmic acceleration is a free parameter to be fitted, or a number fixed in advance by geometry. The framework fixes the dark-energy equation of state algebraically from two dimensionless constants, the golden ratio φ and π, and confronts it without adjustment against DESI DR2 BAO, Planck 2018 and raw weak-lensing and clustering data. The only dimensional input is the measured local expansion rate (SH0ES); at the CMB level only the primordial amplitude A<sub>s</sub> and the optical depth τ are sampled (k = 2 versus 6 for ΛCDM).</p>

<p><strong>Headline.</strong> The equation of state follows as bare ratios of structural invariants, w<sub>0</sub> = {{W0_d3}} and w<sub>a</sub> = {{WA_d3}}, with no fitted amplitude; the point lies {{p2_w0wa_ssee_ec26}}σ from the official DESI DR2 w<sub>0</sub>w<sub>a</sub>CDM posterior (DESI+CMB+Pantheon+; {{p2_w0wa_ssee_ec28}}–{{p2_w0wa_ssee_ec27}}σ for the other supernova compilations). With nothing free (k = 0), model selection against DESI DR2 BAO with a Planck prior gives ΔBIC = {{p2_k0_dBIC_lcdm}} relative to ΛCDM and {{p2_k0_dBIC_cpl}} relative to CPL ({{p2_dBIC_lcdm}} and {{p2_dBIC_cpl}} in the conservative version that samples H<sub>0</sub> and Ω<sub>b</sub>h²; negative favours SSEE). The global expansion rate is the output of a screening cascade run on the SH0ES datum, H<sub>0</sub><sup>glob</sup> = {{H0_GLOBAL_d5}} ± {{p9_hglob_sigma}} km/s/Mpc; the pure number 3(φ+π)² is the comparison target, not an input. The pre-registered falsifiers are the fixed (w<sub>0</sub>, w<sub>a</sub>) point and the tensor ratio r = φ<sup>−10</sup> = {{R_TENSOR_d6}} (LiteBIRD, CMB-S4).</p>

<p><strong>What changed since the previous version (20 July 2026).</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Retracted: the second matter sector and the φ-dark-matter particle</strong> (m<sub>φ</sub> = 40.70 eV) of the former Paper 6, with its free-streaming scale and two-sector S<sub>8</sub>. Its density was defined by subtracting 1+w<sub>0</sub> — an equation-of-state number, not a density — and the S<sub>8</sub> tension it was built to close does not appear in raw data. The model has a single matter density, Ω<sub>m</sub> = {{OMEGA_M_TOTAL_d6}}. Paper 6 is rewritten.</li>
<li><strong>Growth against raw data.</strong> With the amplitude fixed by the model's own CMB fit (no free cosmological parameter), KiDS-Legacy cosmic shear gives S<sub>8</sub> = {{S8_leg_pred}} against a measured {{S8_legacy_dato}} ± {{S8_legacy_dato_sigma}} ({{S8_leg_tension}}σ); fixing it costs nothing (ΔBIC = {{dBIC_leg_libre}} in its favour). KiDS-Legacy predates this analysis and no temporal priority is claimed. Raw BOSS DR12 multipoles: Δχ² = {{bossR_dchi2}} for SSEE at equal freedom.</li>
<li><strong>Direction of the Hubble cascade corrected.</strong> The measured SH0ES rate enters and the global rate comes out; the former local value 72.86 km/s/Mpc read the same statement backwards and is withdrawn. With the infrared term alone the cascade gives {{p9_sh0es_glob_IR}} km/s/Mpc ({{p9_sh0es_sig_IR}}σ from the target); the complete value is conditional on Conjecture C.1 of Paper 10.</li>
<li><strong>Assumption budget stated in full:</strong> four dimensionless postulates — D (dimensional anchor), S (saturation), I (inflationary register) and F (the multiplicative form of the screening, Paper 9) — plus Conjecture C.1, whose dependent results are flagged as conditional.</li>
<li><strong>CMB:</strong> full Planck likelihood (plik TTTEEE + low-ℓ + lensing) with each model at its own minimum, ΔBIC = {{b1_dBIC}} (k = 2 versus 6); the two fits are statistically indistinguishable and the difference is parameter economy. The spectra formerly labelled “Planck PR4” were Planck 2018 (PR3) and are now labelled as such.</li>
<li><strong>Effective field theory:</strong> the dark-energy sector is a two-term k-essence ghost condensate with sound speed c<sub>s</sub>² = {{cs2_condensado_d6}} and kineticity α<sub>K</sub>(0) = {{alpha_K_z0_d6}} (the former 0.4033 was a different quantity). The conformal coupling β<sub>c</sub> = −AURA is withdrawn. Paper 5 is rewritten: dark-energy stability comes from this field, not from the Israel–Stewart limit.</li>
<li><strong>Galaxy clusters:</strong> redone against all 46 systems of Zhang et al. (2026): SSEE {{clz_rgig_sig}}σ, ΛCDM {{clz_lcig_sig}}σ — clusters test the matter content but do not separate the two backgrounds.</li>
<li><strong>Reproducibility:</strong> the numbers in the documents are generated from sealed result files (a DVC pipeline with provenance records), and the few literal values left are checked against their source log; an automated verification suite checks the documents against the code, the logs and each other, with mutation tests showing that each rule detects the defect it is written for.</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>The suite (read in the numbered file order):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Paper 1 — Framework and predictive register:</strong> the algebra, the four postulates, and a register classifying every result as postdiction, retrodiction, prediction or measured input.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 2 — Bayesian validation (DESI DR2 BAO, Planck prior, clusters):</strong> H<sub>0</sub> = {{h0_p2}} ± {{h0_p2_s}} km/s/Mpc; ΔBIC as above.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 3 — CMB:</strong> single matter density, acoustic peaks reproduced; full-likelihood ΔBIC = {{b1_dBIC}}.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 4 — Algebraic derivation of the CMB background:</strong> n<sub>s</sub> = 1 − φ<sup>−7</sup> = {{N_S_d6}}, Ω<sub>b</sub>h², and the 24 additive routes to the maximal invariant.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 5 — Israel–Stewart perturbations:</strong> stability from the field of Paper 7, weak dark-energy clustering, and the phantom crossing as an open problem.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 6 — Growth sector on raw survey data:</strong> one matter sector; KiDS-Legacy, KiDS-1000 and BOSS DR12.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 7 — Effective field theory:</strong> ghost condensate, c<sub>s</sub>² = {{cs2_condensado_d6}}, α<sub>T</sub> = α<sub>M</sub> = α<sub>B</sub> = 0.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 8 — Strong gravity:</strong> GR lensing in the canonical limit; a disformal limit is kept only as a falsifiable contrast.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 9 — Hubble tension:</strong> an algebraic local screening fraction; the cascade from SH0ES.</li>
<li><strong>Paper 10 — UV extension:</strong> K(X) = X/KAL + X²/M⁴ and Conjecture C.1.</li>
<li><strong>Sealed Journal</strong> — the journal-ready document; <strong>Unified Journal</strong> — Papers 1–10 in one narrative; <strong>Endorser Summary</strong>; <strong>Cover Letter</strong>; <strong>PRD submission</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Source archive</strong> — LaTeX, Python, the DVC pipeline with its provenance records, the canonical values file and the verification suite, from commit {{COMMIT}}.</li>
</ul>

<p>Open problems are listed in OPEN_PROBLEMS.md inside the source archive. The structural constant dictionary is a separate record (10.5281/zenodo.20684908).</p>

